603	     * result is that line, with a single space and {@code addressLine2} appended when the second line
604	     * is present; otherwise the flat {@code address} value is used. All three arguments are expected
605	     * to already be normalized (see {@link #normalizeAddress(String)}). This is the single source of
606	     * truth for how an owner's address is read, so every consumer (the stored value and the response)
607	     * sees the structured fields when present and the flat value as the backward-compatible fallback.
