1046	    /**
1047	     * Derive this owner's {@code ownerSegment}, the marketing segment formatted
1048	     * {@code '<TIER>_<AREA>'}. {@code TIER} is {@code 'PREMIUM'} when the owner's effective
1049	     * membership level (see {@link #effectiveMembershipLevel()}) is 3 or more, otherwise
1050	     * {@code 'STANDARD'}. {@code AREA} is {@code 'METRO'} when the owner's locality (see
1051	     * {@link #locality(String)}) is a known region ({@code NSW}, {@code VIC} or {@code QLD}),
1052	     * otherwise {@code 'REGIONAL'}. The result is one of {@code 'PREMIUM_METRO'},
1053	     * {@code 'PREMIUM_REGIONAL'}, {@code 'STANDARD_METRO'} or {@code 'STANDARD_REGIONAL'}.
1054	     *
1055	     * <p>The {@code AREA} is derived from the owner's <em>plain</em> locality region (from the
1056	     * postcode), so the {@link #IDENTITY_VERSION 'V2'} version tag carried inside the identifiers never
1057	     * appears in the owner segment's derived region.
